---
/**
 * Nginx Config Generator Tool Page.
 */
import NginxConfigGeneratorApp from "@components/apps/NginxConfigGenerator.astro";
import ToolLayout from "@layouts/ToolLayout.astro";
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Nginx Config Generator"
  description="Generate Nginx server block configurations with upstream blocks, QUIC/HTTP3, rate limiting, tarpit, OCSP stapling, Brotli, CSP integration, and modern TLS best practices."
  subtitle="Generate production-ready Nginx server blocks with upstream blocks, QUIC/HTTP3, tarpit, rate limiting, and modern TLS best practices."
  icon="i-devicon:nginx"
  slug="nginx-config-generator"
>
  <NginxConfigGeneratorApp title="" />

  <Fragment slot="info">
    <h2>About This Tool</h2>
    <p>
      Generate production-ready Nginx server block configurations with a visual
      builder. Select the features you need and get a complete configuration
      file you can copy directly to your server.
    </p>
    <h3>Features</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>6 presets</strong> — Static, Reverse Proxy, SPA, PHP-FPM, API Server,
        Hardened
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Upstream blocks</strong> — Named upstream with load balancing (round-robin,
        least connections, IP hash), keepalive connections, and multiple backend servers
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Modern SSL/TLS</strong> — QUIC/HTTP3, OCSP stapling, 0-RTT early data,
        strong cipher suites, session tickets off, HSTS preload
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Access control</strong> — Rate limiting with burst, block hidden files,
        block exploit paths (wp-admin, phpMyAdmin), tarpit slow responses
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Security headers</strong> — X-Frame-Options, XCTO, Referrer-Policy,
        Permissions-Policy, COOP/CORP/COEP, basic CSP with link to
        <a href="/tools/csp-builder/">CSP Policy Builder</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Performance</strong> — Gzip, Brotli, static asset caching, open file
        cache, proxy buffering
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Reverse proxy</strong> — WebSocket support, proxy headers, keepalive,
        buffering options
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h3>How to Use</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Start with a preset that matches your use case</li>
      <li>Customize domain, root path, and SSL certificate paths</li>
      <li>Enable QUIC/HTTP3, OCSP stapling, and modern TLS options</li>
      <li>
        Configure access control: rate limiting, blocked paths, and tarpit
      </li>
      <li>Toggle security headers and performance optimizations</li>
      <li>
        Copy the generated configuration and place it in your Nginx sites
        directory
      </li>
    </ol>
    <h3>Learn More</h3>
    <p>
      These blog posts provide detailed guides on the features available in this
      generator:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="/blog/004-enabling-quic-http3-nginx/"
          >Enabling QUIC/HTTP3 in Nginx</a
        > — Configure HTTP/3 and QUIC transport protocol
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/blog/implementing-tarpit-nginx/"
          >Implementing a Tarpit in Nginx</a
        > — Slow down attackers and scanners
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/blog/003-implementing-content-security-policy-nginx/"
          >Implementing CSP in Nginx</a
        > — Content Security Policy configuration
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/blog/001-secure-nginx-client-certificates/"
          >Secure Nginx with Client Certificates</a
        > — Mutual TLS authentication
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
